  "web_source_notes": "Eight active coding hours per person daily on the top model, with no fixed daily question or task allowance. The supplied developer rates of 28 output and 333 new input tokens/s are explicitly assumed throughout active hours; this is not measured Claude usage. One overlapping daily cohort gives an illustrative 610\u2013640k users per campus. The six-campus 500 MW design remains fixed. The requested main-card assumption block is hidden; detailed assumptions remain in AI & energy. A Sundai cover uses a fresh render of the unchanged Blender master. All visible cards, equipment records and design details were audited for superseded annual results. Solar generation and weather availability are separate from operating hours. The hall description clarifies enclosed mineral-wool panels. All 816 dry-cooler and 42 chiller fans animate from Blender-authored rotors. Winter motion is illustrative; real controls can stop fans. The winter card explains heat transport in liquid and the uncalculated worst-case cold-snap heat balance.",
